  "trim": {
    "tolerance": 0.25,
    "small": 24,
    "rule": "Each subpath the ink wrote (absolute M, L and Z only) keeps the fewest of its own points within 0.25 units of every point it had (Ramer-Douglas-Peucker), in whole units when it is at least 24 units across and in tenths when smaller; a subpath that would close on fewer than four points is kept as drawn. Every other path, pattern tile and attribute is kept byte for byte.",
    "evidence": "design/room-drawing/review/renders.json: each export and the untrimmed picture rendered in desktop Chrome at twice their pixels, compared."
  },
